=== verify_2220_family.m ===
(1) generic orders over Q(t): [inf+ - (0,0)] = 5, [(-t-1,.) - (0,0)] = 20
(2) at t = t(z) the quartic factors as (linear)(cubic) over Q(z)
(3) the cover is a singular plane genus-2 curve with normalization Y (conductor 2528)
(4) rank(Jac Y) = 1, torsion Z/4; Chabauty: Y(Q) has exactly 9 points
(5) all rational points of the cover have z in {-1, 0, -1/7, -7/9, oo}; z = -1, 0, oo give t = -1, a degenerate fiber
(6) z = -1/7: fiber isomorphic to Eq.(eq:2220), exact torsion [2,2,20]
(6) z = -7/9: fiber isomorphic to Eq.(eq:2220), exact torsion [2,2,20]
[2,2,20] FAMILY VERIFIED: Eq.(eq:2220) is the unique [2,2,20] member (1.4 s)
=== verify_22212_surface.m ===
(1) Sing(S) = 36 rational points, coordinates in {0,1,-1}
(2) all 36 singular points are ordinary double points
(3) Sing(S) = orbit of [1:0:0:1:0] (12) + orbit of [1:1:0:1:1] (24)
(4) the displayed map sends S into Z (both equations lie in I_S)
SURFACE GEOMETRY VERIFIED (4.0E-2 s)
=== verify_22212_theorem.m ===
point 1 = [ 120, 143, 266, 218, 241 ] lies on S^o
point 1: torsion invariants [ 2, 2, 2, 12 ]
point 1: geometrically simple, witness p=71, chi=x^4 - 8*x^3 + 46*x^2 - 568*x + 5041
point 2 = [ 143, 408, 1015, 437, 1013 ] lies on S^o
point 2: torsion invariants [ 2, 2, 2, 12 ]
point 2: geometrically simple, witness p=37, chi=x^4 - 4*x^3 + 30*x^2 - 148*x + 1369
point 3 = [ 16660, 78793, 21456, 78644, 27593 ] lies on S^o
point 3: torsion invariants [ 2, 2, 2, 12 ]
point 3: geometrically simple, witness p=37, chi=x^4 - 4*x^3 + 30*x^2 - 148*x + 1369
the three curves are pairwise non-isomorphic
THEOREM 3.2 VERIFIED: 3 curves, exact [2,2,2,12], simple, distinct (0.7 s)
=== verify_moduli_identities.m ===
(1) Lemma 2.3(b): 2 D_0 = [(0,0) - infty] generically
(2) Lemma 2.3(d): the four displayed expressions are q(-a_i^2) exactly
(3) Lemma 4.5: (x0,y0) -> ((x0-u)/(x0+u), 2(t+1)y0/(x0+u)^2) maps E_u to V_t
(4) Prop 4.4: all displayed identities hold over Q(s); Lemma 2.3(c) conditions are identically squares
    s = 3 fiber: torsion [ 2, 2, 4, 4 ] contains [2,2,4,4]
(5) Cor 4.3: E_7 has Mordell-Weil rank exactly 1
(6) t = 2 fiber on S: torsion [ 2, 2, 2, 8 ] contains [2,2,2,8]
(6) t = 5 fiber on S: torsion [ 2, 2, 2, 8 ] contains [2,2,2,8]
ALL MODULI IDENTITIES VERIFIED (0.4 s)
